.TH smi-liquibase "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-liquibase \- Run Liquibase database migrations against a PostgreSQL database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-liquibase
.I COMMAND
.RI [ LIQUIBASE_OPTIONS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-liquibase
runs the Liquibase command line installed in
.I /opt/liquibase
with the connection taken
from the
.B SMI_DB_
environment variables, so an administrator can apply, check and revert database changes from the
directory that holds the changelogs.
.PP
Every jar in the
.I jdbc
directory of the SMI lib directory is on the classpath, so a further database is a further driver
package and an
.B SMI_DB_URL
of its own. Every argument is passed to
.BR liquibase ,
so every Liquibase command and option works, and an option given here wins over the one this
command sets.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_DB_HOST
Database host, default
.BR localhost .
.TP
.B SMI_DB_PORT
Database port, default
.BR 5432 .
.TP
.B SMI_DB_NAME
Database name, default
.BR postgres .
.TP
.B SMI_DB_USER
Database user, default
.BR postgres .
.TP
.B SMI_DB_PASSWORD
Password of that user. It reaches Liquibase as
.BR LIQUIBASE_COMMAND_PASSWORD ,
not as an argument, so it is not visible in the process list.
.TP
.B SMI_DB_URL
The whole JDBC URL, replacing the one built from host, port and name, for another database or
for URL parameters.
.TP
.B SMI_DB_CHANGELOG
The entry changelog relative to the working directory, default
.IR db/changelog/db.changelog-master.yaml ,
the default of Spring Boot, so the changelogs of a Spring Boot project work as they are. XML, YAML,
JSON and SQL changelogs are all accepted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/liquibase/
The Liquibase command line, installed by the
.B liquibase
package.
.TP
.I $(smi-lib-location)/jdbc/
The JDBC drivers, installed by the
.B pgjdbc
package for PostgreSQL and the
.B h2
package for H2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.BR liquibase .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show what is not applied yet, apply it, and revert the last change:
.RS
.nf
export SMI_DB_HOST=db.example.com SMI_DB_NAME=app SMI_DB_USER=app_owner
read -rs SMI_DB_PASSWORD; export SMI_DB_PASSWORD
smi-liquibase status --verbose
smi-liquibase update
smi-liquibase rollback-count --count=1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write the SQL an update would run, without running it:
.RS
.nf
smi-liquibase update-sql
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tag the current state, and return to it later:
.RS
.nf
smi-liquibase tag --tag=before-import
smi-liquibase rollback --tag=before-import
.fi
.RE
.PP
Try changelogs on a local H2 database file instead of a server:
.RS
.nf
SMI_DB_URL=jdbc:h2:./trial SMI_DB_USER=sa smi-liquibase update
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-download-package (1),
.BR smi-install-package (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
.SH AUTHOR
setmy.info
